WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.738
Coding Exercise 2 adds filtering to the SELECT
pattern The task is

00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:08.938
to return active patients who are age fifty or older
The output

00:00:08.962 --> 00:00:12.312
should include MRN full name and age and the rows
should be

00:00:12.338 --> 00:00:16.438
sorted by age descending The SELECT list and ORDER
BY clause are

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:20.650
mostly visible in the starter code Your main job is
to complete

00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:26.750
the WHERE condition You need two conditions The
first checks that is_active

00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:30.775
equals true The second checks that age is greater
than or equal

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.475
to fifty Connect them with AND because both
conditions must be satisfied

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.538
Read the condition in plain language before running
it keep a row

00:00:39.562 --> 00:00:42.175
if the patient is active and the age is at least
fifty

00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:47.312
After you select Run and Check inspect the rows Do
not only

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:51.738
rely on the automatic checker Every returned age
should be fifty or

00:00:51.762 --> 00:00:56.375
higher and the result should represent active
patients If too many rows

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.075
appear review the WHERE clause If no rows appear
check whether you

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.338
accidentally used a more restrictive operator or
misspelled a value This exercise

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.625
combines the three most common beginner SQL ideas
choose columns filter rows

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.812
and sort the result
